	1315 [label="You mentioned earlier you wanted to talk about the fact I don't really believe the Indifference is a \"real god.\" Is now a good time?",shape=box,color=red];
		1315 -> 1320;
	1313 [label="[จบ]",shape=box,color=red];
		1313 -> 1318;
	1314 [label="วันก่อนคุณถามผมเรื่องการทำให้แนวคิดกลายเป็นรูปธรรม และเรื่องความเฉยเมย มีอะไรกวนใจคุณหรือเปล่า",shape=box,color=red];
		1314 -> 1319;
	1317 [label="Roathe เชื่อมั่นว่าชายผู้อยู่ในกำแพงไม่ใช่พระเจ้าที่แท้จริง แต่เป็นผลผลิตมาจาก \"การทำให้แนวคิดกลายเป็นรูปธรรม\" คุณคิดอย่างไรกับเรื่องนี้",shape=box,color=red];
		1317 -> 1322;
	1316 [label="Lyon, what's going on between you and Roathe? I've only gleaned bits and pieces.",shape=box,color=red];
		1316 -> 1321;
	1320 [label="I am unsure as any time is a \"good\" time to discuss the tangible problem this has caused me, Drifter.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1320 -> 1324;
	1318 [label="Chat ends.",color=orange];
	1319 [label="มีหลายเรื่องกวนใจผมอยู่นะดริฟเตอร์ ผมเกรงว่าหนึ่งในนั้นจะเป็นเรื่องเกี่ยวกับความเฉยเมยและการทำให้แนวคิดกลายเป็นรูปธรรม",shape=box,color=blue];
		1319 -> 1323;
	1322 [label="The issue at hand, Drifter, is that I do not know. If I knew the answer, I would not be tearing myself apart with such an internal debate.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1322 -> 1326;
	1321 [label="I shall summarize, though I am shocked you have avoided his rants on the topic. He is quite overeager to share them at every opportunity.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1321 -> 1325;
	1324 [label="But as such, now is therefore, as \"good\" a time as any. It intrigued me that you seemed to side with Roathe in your belief that the Indifference was not a true god.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1324 -> 1326;
	1323 [label="Or potentially two, depending on how you wish to interpret the situation. Though I suppose that is indeed the heart of my dilemma.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1323 -> 1326;
	1326 [label="However, I should... start at the beginning. You will not understand precisely why this particular topic is of such import to me if you do not have some context...",shape=box,color=blue];
		1326 -> 1328;
	1325 [label="He believes that the Indifference is not a god of the Void, in any sense of the word, and was in fact crafted by Entrati and all those who interacted with it afterwards -",shape=box,color=blue];
		1325 -> 1327;
	1328 [label="I am a Brother of Lua. I have dedicated my life to her worship. All my life, I have believed this.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1328 -> 1330;
	1327 [label="- สร้างมันขึ้นมาจากวอยด์ผ่านสิ่งที่คุณเรียกว่า \"การทำให้แนวคิดกลายเป็นรูปธรรม\" ",shape=box,color=blue];
		1327 -> 1329;
	1330 [label="And throughout all my years since arriving to the church, I have held fast to my faith - to what has been the firm knowledge that my suffering, my pain, and my visions -",shape=box,color=blue];
		1330 -> 1331;
	1329 [label="Much in the same way you created Duviri, I believe.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1329 -> 1326;
	1331 [label="- have been in her service. Have been in her name. And have been for her purpose.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1331 -> 1332;
	1332 [label="That was... until \"Cardinal Dimanche\" revealed himself to be Albrecht Entrati.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1332 -> 1333;
	1333 [label="And he told us the truth of who he was, the tale of his misdeeds with the Void, and all that came of it. More specifically... all that came out of it.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1333 -> 1334;
		1333 -> 1335;
	1334 [label="The Indifference.",shape=box,color=red];
		1334 -> 1336;
	1335 [label="And?",shape=box,color=red];
		1335 -> 1337;
	1336 [label="Correct. He told us of the sneering thing that greeted him, of the fingers he retrieved from that place that resembled his laboratory.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1336 -> 1338;
	1337 [label="He told us of his descent in the seriglass bell into the emptiness. Of the place that resembled his laboratory. ",shape=box,color=blue];
		1337 -> 1338;
	1338 [label="Moreover, he told us of the great dread he felt, knowing he had unleashed a thing that could follow him not just through space, but through time.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1338 -> 1339;
	1339 [label="A god of nothingness. A thing that must be contained. A creature of which he had pieces, who would scratch at the walls to be freed.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1339 -> 1340;
	1340 [label="A terrible and consuming god who was, and also was not, already free.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1340 -> 1341;
		1340 -> 1342;
	1341 [label="What do you mean?",shape=box,color=red];
		1341 -> 1343;
	1342 [label="\"Was\" and \"also was not\" already freed?",shape=box,color=red];
		1342 -> 1343;
	1343 [label="Check boolean LyonRell1",color=orange];
		1343 -> 1345 [label=true,color=green];
		1343 -> 1344 [label=false,color=brown];
	1345 [label="Time is... tangled, for someone such as I, in the state I am now in. It is hard to describe. I have made a poor attempt to explain this once, and I have failed miserably.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1345 -> 1346;
	1344 [label="Time is... tangled, for someone such as I, in the state I am now in. It is hard to describe, and I am doing a miserable job of it.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1344 -> 1346;
	1346 [label="I would prefer to explain the details of it another time, as that is not the point of what I am trying to get to the heart of this day.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1346 -> 1347;
